      "writtenOn": "2025-10-06T23:51:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It doesn\u0027t really matter because the values we use are in the \"u31\" range. I think it\u0027s good to think of them as signed though because C prior to C23 only requires enums to support the range of `int`, not `unsigned int`. (hence why Force32 is 0x7fff_ffff and not 0xffff_ffff)\n\nMaybe I should have a helper for loading enum values so that the magic \"i32\" is not scattered in every spot.",
